#edb/ref 17592186269237 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186060036 1068 #edb/ref 17592186056544 13194139533401 17592186045585 false] [17592186060036 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268725 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186060036 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186060036 1071 "Let $u = ⟨ - 3, 2⟩$ and $v = ⟨7, 9⟩$. Find $u \\cdot v$." 13194139533401 17592186045585 false] [17592186060036 1071 "Let $u=⟨-3,2⟩$ and $v=⟨7,9⟩.$ Find $u\\cdot v.$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186060036 1074 "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot 7+2\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =-21+18 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186068922 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269136 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186068923 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269009 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186068923 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269039 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186068923 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269051 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186069052 1068 #edb/ref 17592186065715 13194139533401 17592186045585 false] [17592186069052 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268454 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186069052 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186069052 1071 "$\\int 4{x}^{2}{sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186069052 1071 "What is $\\displaystyle \\int4x^{2}\\sec^{2} (x^{3})dx$?" 13194139533401 17592186045585 false] [17592186069052 1074 "Let $u={x}^{3}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{x}^{2}{sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int {sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186069053 1068 #edb/ref 17592186065721 13194139533401 17592186045585 false] [17592186069053 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268434 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186069053 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186069053 1071 "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186069053 1071 "What is $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π/8}5\\sin (4x)dx$?" 13194139533401 17592186045585 false] [17592186069053 1074 "If we let $u=4x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi /8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186073721 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269110 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186083312 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269109 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186083330 1038 #edb/ref 17592186268917 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186083332 1038 #edb/ref 17592186268923 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186083332 1038 #edb/ref 17592186268931 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186083335 1038 #edb/