 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269136 1072 #uuid "996adb7b-cb39-5733-9d5d-ec3bcfe1a670" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269136 1074 "If we let $u=3x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /9$ | $\\pi /6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /3$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /9}^{\\pi /6}2{csc}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}2{csc}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡u{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(0-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269137 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268809 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269137 1069 "q-136631" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269137 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269137 1071 "If $sec⁡a=-8,$ then $sec⁡(-a)=$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269137 1072 #uuid "a2a3460c-5045-59bc-aae3-13b2bea30fac" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269137 1074 "First, let's recall the graph of $y=sec⁡x.$\n\n![](images/fb/fbf6ef1ca91f998ab4dc2dda1890ffc8a713f2eeff19e5569351b2466256d63a.png)\n\nNotice that our graph is symmetric about the $y$-axis. If we reflect the graph about the $y$-axis, we get the same picture. This means that $sec⁡x$ is an *even* function, and we have\n\n$$\nsec⁡(-x)=sec⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sec⁡(-a) & =sec⁡a \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269138 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268793 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269138 1069 "q-136639" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269138 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269138 1071 "If $tan⁡a=\\frac{4}{5},$ then $tan⁡(-a)=$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269138 1072 #uuid "b5606ff1-4177-5d4b-892b-30b0ba862cf3" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269138 1074 "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/df/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nOur graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{∘}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-a) & =-tan⁡a \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269139 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268536 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269139 1069 "q-136811" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269139 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269139 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $b$ above. If the normal equation corresponding to the system $Ax=b$ is given below, what is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 20 \\\\ 20 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269139 1072 #uuid "d00d21df-b149-5102-8948-a439a72941dc" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269139 1074 "The normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}10 & 20 \\\\ 20 & 40\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=10+40+(-2)=48.\n$$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269140 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268444 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269140 1069 "q-136822" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269140 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269140 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ -6{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}40 & -20 & -60 \\\\ -20 & 10 & a \\\\ c & 30 & 90\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ b \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations and its corresponding normal equation shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269140 1072 #uuid "69f4362f-6b4d-5c30-8b5c-dedd940a5e83" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269140 1074 "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}40 & 20 & -60 \\\\ -20 & 10 & 30 \\\\ -60 & 30 & 90\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}