onding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -15 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -5) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =-3,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}=5.\n$$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269173 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268459 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269173 1069 "q-138067" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269173 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269173 1071 "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269173 1072 #uuid "0245ff8a-62ef-503c-845b-a63c21512dda" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269173 1074 "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A