 $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\n \nThe minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}=-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-1)I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-1))x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{min}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269181 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268663 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269181 1069 "q-13809" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269181 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269181 1071 "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269181 1072 #uuid "9dd71bce-d500-5352-b13b-ce18dffed7d4" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269181 1074 "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{u}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269182 1068 #edb/ref 1759