}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}y\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{({e}^{t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{e}^{2t}}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269209 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268418 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269209 1069 "q-13911" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269209 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269209 1071 "Find the first three non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion of ${e}^{-{x}^{3}}$ about $x=-1.$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269209 1072 #uuid "9199b761-5297-59d6-ae88-d4d8a0096e50" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269209 1074 "We use Taylor's theorem in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $f(x)={e}^{-{x}^{3}}$ and $a=-1.$ \n\nComputing the required derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{-{x}^{3}} \\\\ f(-1) & ={e}^{-(-1)^{3}}=e \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-3{x}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =-3(-1)^{2}{e}^{-(-1)^{3}}=-3e \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =(-3{x}^{2})\\cdot (-3{x}^{2})\\cdot {e}^{-{x}^{3}}+(-6x)\\cdot {e}^{-{x}^{3}}=(9{x}^{4}-6x){e}^{-{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(-1) & =(9\\cdot (-1)^{4}-6\\cdot (-1)){e}^{-(-1)^{3}}=15e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-{x}^{3}} & =e+(-3e)(x+1)+\\frac{15e}{2!}(x+1)^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =e-3e(x+1)+\\frac{15e}{2}(x+1)^{2}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269210 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268619 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269210 1069 "q-1392" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269210 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269210 1071 "Let $a=2i-3j+5k$ and $b=-i+4j+3k.$ Determine $a\\times b.$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269210 1072 #uuid "17b9a485-4825-5256-b837-58364fae905a" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269210 1074 "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-3\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 4)i-(2\\cdot 3-5\\cdot (-1))j+(2\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =(-9-20)i-(6-(-5))j+(8-3)k \\\\  & =-29i-11j+5k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269211 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268801 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269211 1069 "q-139243" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269211 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269211 1071 "Which of the following data sets **might** be normally distributed?" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269211 1072 #uuid "45441f69-eba6-5e77-85da-92d44bcba204" 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269211 1074 "If a large data set is normally distributed, it should be approximately bell-shaped. \n\nAmong the given options, the only bell-shaped curve is the following:\n\n![](images/d1/d1fe4e44e042a17e8e5e827851137568ee39d58b0747e4a9a12dd8e0c22679b3.png)\n\nIt's important to note that other bell-shaped distributions exist. Therefore, further tests on the data are required to confirm whether the underlying distribution is normal." 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269212 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268591 13194139533401 17592186045585 true] [17592186269212 1069 "q-139244" 13194139